          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "{\"events\":[{\"id\":884,\"name\":\"Handsworth Songs\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-22T14:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-22T17:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"beef0def17786822e926dba2565f52fc.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"An experimental documentary depicting protests around the UK, positioning the camera with the protesters rather than pointed at them.\\n\\n\\nHandsworth Songs (1986, 61 mins) is an experimental documentary depicting the lives of those in Handsworth, Brixton, and Tottenham during three different people’s uprisings in 1985, positioning the camera with the protesters rather than pointed at them.\\n\\nProduced by Black Audio Film Collective, Handsworth Songs interrogates the impact of colonialism and what it means to be Black-British at a time when these two terms were, and still are, at odds with each other.\\n\\nWhilst made for the television screen, Handsworth Songs has gone on to be screened in museums and art houses around the world. Following this screening we will hold a community conversation to mark the 15 year anniversary of Mark Duggan's death which caused uprisings across London and spread to other parts of England. We aim to consider how the riots of 1985 and 2011 are similar and different, understanding how they changed the course of history and also the way in which we, as an organisation in Haringey, interact with the history of the borough.\\n\\n\\n\\nThis is the third and final screening of HCC's Summer Programme: Making the Revolution Irresistible\\n\\nAbout the film \\u0026 filmmakers\\nTrailer\\n\\n\\nAWARDS:\\n\\nBritish Film Institute Grierson Award for Best Documentary in 1986.\\n\\nJOHN AKOMFRAH: Director\\n\\nFounder of Black Audio Film Collective, Akomfrah is a filmmaker who experiments with textures and sounds to create a landscape which explores the many outcomes of colonialism and immigration. Beginning with a career in television, via Chanel 4’s Workshop schemes, Akomfrah has more recently gone on to create installation pieces for art centres and museums internationally.\\n\\nOther works include:\\n\\nSeven Songs for Malcom X (1993)\\n\\nThe Stuart Hall Project (2013)\\n\\nThe Last Angel of History (1996)\\n\\n\\n\\nAbout our Guest Speaker\\n\\n\\nGuest Speaker: TBC\\n\\nBooking / Waiting List / Cancellation\\n\\n\\nPlease only book if you are confident you will be able to attend, as seating at this venue is limited. Due to safety regulations, walk-in entry cannot be guaranteed.\\n\\nThe registration form includes a small number of questions collected for reporting purposes. All data will be anonymised. Each attendee is required to complete the form. If you are booking on behalf of someone else and do not know an answer, please enter or select' N/A' where applicable.\\n\\nDue to the venue’s limited capacity, the event may sell out.If this happens, you can be added to the waiting list. When a ticket becomes available, you will receive an email to book it, and you will have 24 hours to complete your booking.\\n\\nIf you are unable to attend the event, please cancel your ticket(s) so that your place can be offered to someone else.\\n\\nWhy your donations are important?\\n\\nPlease read carefully! We’re introducing a Community Pricing to help cover the costs of our events. Choose the ticket tier that best reflects your current circumstances— considering income, housing, caring responsibilities, health, and day-to-day financial pressures. We trust you to choose what feels right. More on this system here.\\n\\nHCC is run by volunteers and does not receive any funding at the moment. Every donation you make will help us to support local venues and to organise other free screenings.\\n\\nIn a time of rising living costs and persistent barriers for marginalised communities in producing and accessing films that reflect their experiences and aspirations, we are committed to making our screenings free or pay-what-you-can.\\n\\nAbout the venue\\n\\nLordship Hub is a vibrant community centre and café at the heart of Lordship Rec, Tottenham’s largest park. The building is fully accessible, but located inside the park. If you need to be dropped off next to the building's main entrance (with the ramp), please contact us early so we can arrange the park's gate to be open. If you have any accessibility needs or questions, please contact us at haringeycommunitycinema@gmail.com.\\n\\nAbout HCC\\n\\nHaringey Community Cinema (HCC) was launched in April 2025 and is run by volunteers. Inspired by Brixton Community Cinema, HCC is aimed at bringing residents of Haringey together through film. Our mission is to showcase films that challenge, inspire, and spark critical reflection—films that make us think and act. Visit our website.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nCovid Policy\\n\\nHCC does not currently have an official COVID-19 policy. However, we remain mindful that many people are still vulnerable to the virus. We kindly ask attendees to take the following precautions to help keep our events safe and accessible for everyone:\\n\\nIf possible, please take a lateral flow test before attending.\\nIf you test positive or are experiencing any COVID-19 symptoms, please do not attend, even if you feel well.\\nWe welcome and encourage the use of masks inside the venue for those who wish to wear them.\\nPlease be considerate of others' comfort levels and respect requests for physical distance.\\nThank you for helping us create a safer and more inclusive space.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/handsworth-songs-registration-1995292310011\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"}],\"is_free\":true,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":143,\"name\":\"Lordship Hub\",\"address\":\"Lordship Rec, Off Higham Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":199,\"name\":\"Haringey Community Cinema\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":22,\"name\":\"documentary\"},{\"id\":214,\"name\":\"Black British history\"},{\"id\":619,\"name\":\"Black Audio Film Collective\"}]},{\"id\":889,\"name\":\"Everybody to Kenmure Street - Community Screening with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-25T18:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-25T21:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"104a0792fcafc92cfc51e8b13d4dca64.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"In May 2021, a UK Home Office dawn raid triggers one of the most spontaneous and successful acts of civil resistance in recent memory. In Pollokshields, Scotland’s most diverse neighbourhood, hundreds of residents rush to the streets to stop the deportation of their neighbours. In today’s increasingly far-right political environment of immigration raids, deportation flights and border violence, Everybody to Kenmure Street is an empowering reminder of the importance of collective action.\\n\\n \\n\\nThe screening will be followed by a casual chat with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids @slantiraids on the organising they do in the area, and how you can get involved.\\n\\n \\n\\nAll are welcome, no matter your organising experience! The film is rated 12A.\\n\\n \\n\\nPay What You Can tickets are available from £1-8. This event is part of a series of community screenings around London with local anti raids groups, organised by april forrest lin 林森. All ticket revenue will be donated to Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids after event costs have been covered.\\n\\n \\n\\n18:30 - Doors open\\n\\n19:00 - Film screening\\n\\n20:45 - Chat with Southwark and Lambeth Anti Raids\\n\\n21:00 - Chat ends, space stays open\\n\\n21:30 - Event ends\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/38273/everybody-to-kenmure-street-community-screening-with-southwark-and-lambeth-anti-raids\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":41,\"name\":\"SET Social\",\"address\":\"55a Nigel Road\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":155,\"name\":\"screening\"},{\"id\":195,\"name\":\"migrant rights\"},{\"id\":222,\"name\":\"community\"},{\"id\":623,\"name\":\"anti-raids\"},{\"id\":624,\"name\":\"collective action\"}]},{\"id\":867,\"name\":\"Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. \\u0026 feeo\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-27T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-27T23:30:00Z\",\"poster\":\"bb5623d6a6a9d23b79385cc4eb6cb434.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"\\nPresenting a double bill of vanguard techno producer Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. and vocalist and producer feeo at Ormside on Thursday 27th August. Ahead of carnival weekend celebrations and commemorations, we welcome two artists whose practices channel experiences of blackness via the collapsing and re-contextualisation of diasporic music idioms.\\n\\nWelcoming Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. to Ormside for his first UK show in a decade. A 90s veteran of UK techno, Alfa embodies resilience, having overcome serious health issues and systemic obstacles over the past few years. In response, his newest work ‘Infinite Black Inside’ (FO) tenderly serves fractured pulses and bass-heavy experiments, drawing on a full spectrum of radical Black music and a lifetime of experience. Free Jazz meets footwork, techno and dub – filtered through Alfa’s own lens to form a sonic imprint entirely his own, imbued with hope.\\n\\nfeeo is the solo project of London-based artist and vocalist Theodora Laird. Working across electronics, written word and performance – feeo investigates the feedback and tension between personal and political story. In her 2025 debut album ‘Goodness’ (AD93), feeo explores opposing forces of darkness and lightness, delivered via static hum, tape drones and whispers of dance music forms. On the 27th feeo presents a new solo performance at Ormside – her first London show since headlining ICA in February of this year.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"gig\"},{\"id\":3,\"name\":\"exhibition\"},{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":1639,\"artist_name\":\"feeo\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2236,\"artist_name\":\"Ibrahim Alfa\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":2,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"address\":\"Penarth Centre, 32 Ormside Street\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"U.K.\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":53,\"name\":\"Ormside Projects\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":777,\"name\":\"1st Release\",\"price\":13,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":15,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":true,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":778,\"name\":\"2nd release\",\"description\":\"\\nPresenting a double bill of vanguard techno producer Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. and vocalist and producer feeo at Ormside on Thursday 27th August. Ahead of carnival weekend celebrations and commemorations, we welcome two artists whose practices channel experiences of blackness via the collapsing and re-contextualisation of diasporic music idioms.\\n\\nWelcoming Ibrahim Alfa Jnr. to Ormside for his first UK show in a decade. A 90s veteran of UK techno, Alfa embodies resilience, having overcome serious health issues and systemic obstacles over the past few years. In response, his newest work ‘Infinite Black Inside’ (FO) tenderly serves fractured pulses and bass-heavy experiments, drawing on a full spectrum of radical Black music and a lifetime of experience. Free Jazz meets footwork, techno and dub – filtered through Alfa’s own lens to form a sonic imprint entirely his own, imbued with hope.\\n\\nfeeo is the solo project of London-based artist and vocalist Theodora Laird. Working across electronics, written word and performance – feeo investigates the feedback and tension between personal and political story. In her 2025 debut album ‘Goodness’ (AD93), feeo explores opposing forces of darkness and lightness, delivered via static hum, tape drones and whispers of dance music forms. On the 27th feeo presents a new solo performance at Ormside – her first London show since headlining ICA in February of this year.\",\"price\":15.2,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":15,\"quantity_sold\":0,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"depends_on_tier_id\":777,\"dependency_sold_out\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":false,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":8,\"name\":\"experimental\"}]},{\"id\":852,\"name\":\"Threshold Houseboys Choir: Form Grows Rampant\",\"start_time\":\"2026-08-29T19:30:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-29T22:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"283b6a5f96330153f6b1882cdaad3f0e.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"A very rare screening of the now out of print DVD film of Peter Christopherson’s solo project ‘Threshold Houseboys Choir’ Form Grows Rampant.\\n\\n\\\"In 2003 I was invited to attend the Ginjae Festival in Krabi Town in the south of Thailand. Ginjae literally means vegetarian, though the connection is obscure. \\n\\nThe major celebrations of this festival take place on the nearby island of Phuket, but there, the atmosphere is one of spectacle, rather than purpose. I had been told about a very different celebration, based around a small chinese shrine or holy place, behind a Toyota dealership in Krabi Town, some 50 kilometres from Phuket island, on the mainland. The Ginjae Festival takes place on the 9th full moon of the year. Over the course of ten days (during which participants wear white and abstain from meat, alcohol and sex) a series of rituals are performed. intended to keep the world spinning on the correct axis. To bring merit and good luck to the village, and to scare away malign spirits that might otherwise bring misfortune to the neighbourhood; especially at busy intersections, accident black spots, etc... \\n\\nThe participants setting out from the shrine we visited were all young men, led by a young 'khatoey\\\" holy man. For the most part they were tattooed tearaways or troublemakers and not the kind of person you would expect to see the local shop-keepers on their knees praying to by the side of the road. In all cases that I witnessed, the rituals were carried out while the participants were in trance or possessed states; often lasting several hours. The boys were trained in, and induced into these states by their holy man, in whom they had complete trust. \\n\\nRemoved from immediate contact with the present by these mental states, the boys seemed not to feel pain. Though as their expressions show, this was not always the case when the trance weakened. Their trances also assisted their speedy recovery - along with the ice-water that their assistants poured on their wounds from kettles throughout the ritual. I saw most of these boys in the days that followed and they appeared to have suffered no ill-effects. and indeed to be almost completely scar free. Certainly emotionally they seemed buoyed by events, as did the worshippers in the neighbourhoods they passed through. \\n\\nBy contrast I was admitted to hospital for several days, suffering from some undiagnosed disorder, which I ascribe to temporarily becoming inadvertent host to one of the evil spirits that their rituals disturbed. \\n\\nIn this work my interpretation of the rituals - my focus and my music - ape entirely personal, and not directly connected to purpose of the Ginjae Festival. I simply believe I saw and filmed something profound, transcendent; the deity incarnate even; in the most unlikely of settings and want to share that with you. \\n\\nAs Jhonn said: \\\"We all get the gods we deserve...\\\"\\n\\n- Peter Christopherson Bangkok January 3rd 2007\\n\\nScreening starts at 8:30pm.\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":false,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"artists\":[{\"id\":2197,\"artist_name\":\"Peter Christopherson\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2198,\"artist_name\":\"Coil\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"},{\"id\":2199,\"artist_name\":\"Threshold Houseboys Choir\",\"gov_name\":\"\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"bio\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"venues\":[{\"id\":17,\"name\":\"The Horse Hospital\",\"address\":\"Colonnade\",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":136,\"name\":\"The Horse Hospital\",\"contact_email\":\"\",\"stripe_account_id\":\"\",\"ticket_email\":\"\",\"custom_domain\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"ticket_tiers\":[{\"id\":752,\"name\":\"General Admission\",\"price\":10,\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"quantity_available\":90,\"quantity_sold\":3,\"resale_listed_count\":0,\"hidden\":false,\"password_protected\":false,\"is_pwyc\":false,\"is_free\":false,\"resale_enabled\":true,\"resale_when_event_sold_out\":true,\"sort_order\":0,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"tags\":[{\"id\":607,\"name\":\"coil\"}]},{\"id\":858,\"name\":\"Tufan ~ Closing Party ☆\",\"start_time\":\"2026-09-05T15:00:00Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-09-06T03:00:00Z\",\"poster\":\"3eecd5307f3644a89795b96c79f17723.webp\",\"background\":\"\",\"description\":\"To celebrate the ending of Tufan and Oitij-jo’s participation in Backyard Biennial: East, we are throwing the official big 12 hour closing party! \\n\\nFeaturing Art, Films, Zines, Workshop, DJs + Open Decks (BRING YOUR USB)!\\n\\nLineup: \\n\\nKhan-Ki featuring Alex Neon\\nMisbah\\nAmena Zaman\\nbkonsmoke (Ace.RGB B2B M4ria B2B frostfight000)\\n\\n3pm - 5pm ~ Film Screenings\\n\\n5pm - 7pm ~ T-Shirt Printing Workshop\\n\\n7pm - 8pm ~ Open Decks\\n\\n8pm - 3am ~ DJs\\n\\n9pm ~ Artwork Sales End\\n\\n+ More information about the programme to be announced…\\n\",\"is_featured\":false,\"poster_small\":\"\",\"is_preview\":false,\"external_url\":\"\",\"is_announced\":true,\"is_on_listings_site\":true,\"resale_queue_enabled\":true,\"is_test_event\":false,\"is_cancelled\":false,\"categories\":[{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"film\"},{\"id\":9,\"name\":\"workshop\"}],\"is_free\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":156,\"name\":\"Oitij-jo Arts Space\",\"address\":\"Unit 3, Lighterman House, 3 Clove Crescent \",\"city\":\"London\",\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"capacity\":0,\"contact_email\":\"\",\"on_listings_site\":false,\"wheelchair_accessible\":false,\"accessible_bathrooms\":false,\"hearing_loop\":false,\"accessible_parking\":false,\"lift_access\":false,\"date_created\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"date_updated\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\"}],\"promoters\":[{\"id\":255